# game.saves = files: a pin from the F1 Saves page at the main menu reaches the game as a hot swap once the overlay
# closes (docs/port/SAVES.md 5.1). Run by tools/port/saves_check.py's swap scenario, which fills the folder first with
# two ghosts of one player, track and way (one note name: the faster on the pak) and checks that the slower one,
# pinned here, is on the pak after the swap and the game read it again.
# until: 0x10:200
# seconds: 60
# realtime
# args: --saves files (tools/port/saves_check.py runs it, in a data folder of its own)
5 A            # the controller pak warning
8 START        # the start prompt; the main menu (0x10) from about 8 s
10 MENU        # F1 over the main menu
10.6 DOWN 0.1  # Video, Audio, Keyboard, Controllers, Game, Mods, Saves
10.9 DOWN 0.1
11.2 DOWN 0.1
11.5 DOWN 0.1
11.8 DOWN 0.1
12.0 DOWN 0.1
12.2 A 0.1     # the Saves page: Player, Kept as, Folder, Import ghosts, Export to the .mpk, then the saves
12.6 DOWN 0.1
12.9 DOWN 0.1
13.2 DOWN 0.1
13.5 DOWN 0.1
13.8 DOWN 0.1
14.1 DOWN 0.1  # the second ghost, the slower
14.5 A 0.1     # its page: Kind, Player, Track, Time, Car, Pages, On the pak, File, Pin to the pak
14.9 DOWN 0.1
15.2 DOWN 0.1
15.5 DOWN 0.1
15.8 DOWN 0.1
16.1 DOWN 0.1
16.4 DOWN 0.1
16.7 DOWN 0.1
17.0 DOWN 0.1
17.4 A 0.1     # pinned
18 START       # the overlay closes; the pak goes out at the next flush and back in after the game's poll
